Read one retained verification failure's owner item, or decide it. An approval
asks the manager to admit the one linked verification/review-only successor; a
denial or a hold launches nothing.

positional arguments:
  {recovery-item,recovery-decide}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --store STORE         the Job store the recovery records live in
  --authority-uuid AUTHORITY_UUID
                        the 32-lowercase-hex Authority this Job store belongs
                        to
  --incarnation INCARNATION
                        this process's incarnation, which is what restart
                        recovery distinguishes managers by
  --control CONTROL     the Worker Manager control store, opened READ-ONLY:
                        the retained candidate and the delivered diagnosis are
                        read through their owner, and a decision must not be
                        able to change the evidence it is judging
  --authority AUTHORITY
                        the Authority store whose Work this failure ran under;
                        it resolves the deciding participant's principal and
                        the Work's own effective scope, and this command
                        writes nothing to it
  --instance INSTANCE   the deployment's state root, whose own layout and
                        emitted configuration say which stores and which
                        Authority it owns and whose selector is asked whether
                        a worker can serve the successor's review stage
  --owners OWNERS       the deployment's owner-port factory as
                        module:attribute; it composes the owner authorization,
                        the host exclusion, the Work authorization, the
                        deployment binding and the instance guard over this
                        instance's own stores
  --failure FAILURE     the failure key Stage 1-A attributed this ending under

recovery-item:
  --participant PARTICIPANT
                        the acting participant. On recovery-item it is
                        optional and reports whether that address holds the
                        decision capability in the Work's own scope; on
                        recovery-decide it is required and there is
                        deliberately no --actor
  --control-report      also report the failed Job's own LIM-5 control and
                        whichever fence closed it

recovery-decide:
  --decision-id DECISION_ID
                        the owner's own operation key. The same key with the
                        same operands replays the committed decision; with
                        different operands it collides, and a later
                        disposition is a NEW key and a new attributable act
  --approve             approve the exact correction and the
                        verification/review-only scope below
  --deny                deny it; nothing is launched
  --hold                hold it for a later explicit disposition; nothing is
                        launched
  --expect-failure-digest EXPECT_FAILURE_DIGEST
                        the fixed input digest the delivered analysis was
                        admitted on
  --expect-report-digest EXPECT_REPORT_DIGEST
                        the delivered diagnosis's own digest; omitted for a
                        finite analysis ending, which delivered partial
                        evidence and no report
  --expect-candidate-base EXPECT_CANDIDATE_BASE
  --expect-candidate-head EXPECT_CANDIDATE_HEAD
  --expect-candidate-digest EXPECT_CANDIDATE_DIGEST
                        the retained candidate's measured content digest; a
                        commit name alone is not a candidate
  --original-verification WORD
                        one argument word of the command that FAILED,
                        repeatable in order (write a word that starts with a
                        dash as --original-verification=-m)
  --corrected-verification WORD
                        one argument word of the APPROVED corrected command,
                        repeatable in order. Approving the command that failed
                        is refused as the generic retry it is
  --context-digest CONTEXT_DIGEST
                        the approved execution context's digest; a command
                        string must not hide a changed working directory,
                        environment or tool selection
  --profile PROFILE     the owner-approved finite profile identity
  --profile-digest PROFILE_DIGEST
                        that profile definition's exact digest; admission
                        checks exact agreement
  --stage STAGE         one selected stage word, repeatable in order:
                        verification then review, or review alone under a
                        review-only decision. implementation is refused by
                        name
  --prior-successor PRIOR_SUCCESSOR
                        the expired successor a review-only decision follows
  --prior-verification-attempt PRIOR_VERIFICATION_ATTEMPT
                        that successor's verification attempt identity
  --prior-verification-digest PRIOR_VERIFICATION_DIGEST
                        the digest of its journalled passed verification
                        account
usage: manager recovery [-h] --store STORE --authority-uuid AUTHORITY_UUID
                        --incarnation INCARNATION --control CONTROL
                        --authority AUTHORITY --instance INSTANCE
                        [--owners OWNERS] --failure FAILURE
                        [--participant PARTICIPANT] [--control-report]
                        [--decision-id DECISION_ID] [--approve | --deny |
                        --hold]
                        [--expect-failure-digest EXPECT_FAILURE_DIGEST]
                        [--expect-report-digest EXPECT_REPORT_DIGEST]
                        [--expect-candidate-base EXPECT_CANDIDATE_BASE]
                        [--expect-candidate-head EXPECT_CANDIDATE_HEAD]
                        [--expect-candidate-digest EXPECT_CANDIDATE_DIGEST]
                        [--original-verification WORD]
                        [--corrected-verification WORD]
                        [--context-digest CONTEXT_DIGEST] [--profile PROFILE]
                        [--profile-digest PROFILE_DIGEST] [--stage STAGE]
                        [--prior-successor PRIOR_SUCCESSOR]
                        [--prior-verification-attempt PRIOR_VERIFICATION_ATTEMPT]
                        [--prior-verification-digest PRIOR_VERIFICATION_DIGEST]
                        {recovery-item,recovery-decide}

